===== plan-amendment-cycle035.md =====
# Plan amendment — Cycle 035 (jev-plan-exit REVISE + jev-observe-exit charges, APPLIED before any build script)

Filed FIRST in Execute, per the Cycle 035 Wave 32 RUN.md §2b disposition for T190. The Cycle-034 item record (`runs/2026-11-18-cycle-034-wave-31/item-T190-observe-plan.md`) is the Execute authority AS AMENDED by this file. Source: `runs/2026-11-18-cycle-035-wave-32/RUN.md` §2b (jev-plan-exit: T190 REVISE, primary class UNBOUND-SCHEDULE; jev-observe-exit: ADVANCE-WITH-GAPS with the frame-resolution charge).

## Amendments applied

1. **Turn windows, scale curve and the couch's internal turn move INTO the five scene objects.** Each entry of CONFIG `scenes` now carries its own `turnStartMs`, `readableMs`, `turnOutStartMs`, `turnOutEndMs`, `scalePeak` and `scalePeakMs` (derived, see 2), and the couch scene additionally carries `profileTurnStartMs` + `profileReadableMs` for its internal turn. No turn/scale timing lives in the animation logic or in loose top-level timeline literals beyond the shared defaults (`turnDeg`, `turnDir`, `turnEasing`, `pivot`, `perspectivePx`, `scalePeakAt`) that the scene objects consume.

2. **Observed turn + crop asserted at 7,000 ms and 9,000 ms.** CP4 evaluates at the BLANK caption midpoint (7,000 ms) asserting phase == TURN (camera turn-in start). CP5 evaluates at the census instant 9,000 ms — `scenes[3].scalePeakMs`, derived as `turnOutStartMs + scalePeakAt × (turnOutEndMs − turnOutStartMs)` = 8000 + 0.5 × 2000 = 9,000 ms — asserting the TRANSFORMED bounds crop the top edge (top < 0) with the caption-safe band intact (bottom < stageHPx − captionSafeBandPx). f010 at 9,000 ms is priced as a rotating cropped form, NOT a camera hold: the camera scene's turn-out window is [8000, 10000] ms, so 9,000 ms is mid-turn-out at the scale peak. The crop check sits at the census instant.

3. **Frame-resolution refinement narrows windows only after a consistent default stands.** The plan §3 check over 8.5–10.0 s runs FIRST against the default above (turn-out [8000,10000], peak at 9,000 ms); it may narrow `turnOutStartMs`/`turnOutEndMs` only if the sampled frames contradict the default, and any re-anchor is recorded in build-record.md with the sampled evidence. (Executed: see build-record.md §Frame-resolution — the sampled frames CONTRADICTED a crop at exactly 9,000 ms: at 9.0 s the form's top edge is still 112 px inside the frame; the first sampled crop is at 9.5 s. The crop probe was therefore RE-ANCHORED to 9,500 ms — recorded here to reconcile this amendment with the build record, per the jev-prewave HOLD finding 3: 9,500 ms is the first sampled crop and the chosen build anchor; the source's true peak instant is UNVERIFIED, because the whole-frame white-pixel statistic does not isolate the icon and is larger again at 9.75 s. The 9,000 ms instant keeps its own assertion (CP5b: rotating form mid-turn), derived from the CONFIG turn-out window midpoint.)

4. **Six-pose-rows vs five-scenes count resolved.** The census names six readable poses (globe · ear · CC badge · film camera · couch front three-quarter · couch profile). CONFIG `scenes` holds FIVE scene objects; the sixth pose (couch profile) is the couch scene's `mapProfile`, reached by that scene's internal turn — it is not a sixth scene. Count assertion (A9.3): scenes == 5, readable poses == 6 (5 × mapFront + couch mapProfile), captions == 6 entries (5 lines + 1 BLANK).

5. **CP7's `profileReadableMs` enters the scene schema.** It is a field of the couch scene object (`scenes[4].profileReadableMs` = 13000); CP7 evaluates at that CONFIG field. It does not leave CP7.

6. **`beatScale` default + one scaling/rounding rule for all boundary checks.** CONFIG carries `beatScale: 1`. RULE (the only scaling rule): every CONFIG timeline instant (scene turn/readable/turn-out/profile instants, caption fromMs/toMs, captionOnlyMs, endMs, and every CP evaluation instant derived from them) is multiplied by `beatScale` and rounded with Math.round to integer ms; a "just before" boundary check (CP1) evaluates at (scaled instant − 1 ms), the 1 ms offset applied AFTER scaling and rounding. At beatScale 0.8: CP1 1999 → 1599, CP8 13917 → 11134. The swap harness asserts both the moved instants and the expected states at them.

7. **CP7 profile readability also asserts the "?"** — the profile map includes the seated figure and the "?" glyph as code-authored pixels of `mapProfile`; CP7 asserts activeMap == couch.mapProfile (which contains them by construction) and captionAt(t) == L5.

Retained from the plan unchanged: segment-anchored schedule basis; caption single-slot half-open schedule ([0,4000) L1 · [4000,6000) L2 · [6000,8000) BLANK · [8000,10000) L3 · [10000,12000) L4 · [12000,13917) L5); the frame-resolution check over 8.5–10.0 s before fixing scalePeakMs (executed per amendment 3); swap values (71-char L3 replacement · beatScale 0.8 · ink #ffd23f); five-lens estimate and plateau pricing.

===== A6 leg 1: fit-table.md (VERBATIM) =====
# fit-table — T190 pixel-icon cold open (guard-measured-fit, A6 pre-wave leg; cured form after jev-prewave HOLD finding 2)

Method: PIL glyph measurement with DejaVu Sans Mono as the Courier-class monospace stand-in (fleet precedent T57: stand-in font, post-fit wrapped geometry, PIXEL-UNVERIFIED — no browser route from this seat). Font: DejaVuSansMono.ttf at CONFIG `captionFontPx` 28; measured advance 16.8594 px → factor 0.6021 (CONFIG carries 0.6023). Each row is a POST-LAYOUT measurement: the line as the build's `captionLayout` actually lays it out (word-boundary two-line split minimizing the longest line; fit-shrink of fontPx when the best split still exceeds avail), rendered to a bitmap and measured (ink bbox). Container avail = stageWPx 640 − 2×captionPadPx 6 = 628 px. Ink height also printed at the 360 px stage (×360/640). Raw measurement output is filed verbatim in build-record.md.

| element (layout line) | container | measured ink bounds | container bounds | margin (binding side) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| L1 line 1 "MORE THAN 430 MILLION PEOPLE" | caption band | 470 px wide · ink height 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px avail · band 64 px | 158 px |
| L1 line 2 "WITH DISABLING HEARING LOSS" | caption band | 453 px · 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 175 px |
| L2 line 1 "RELY ON CAPTIONS TO" | caption band | 318 px · 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 310 px |
| L2 line 2 "WATCH MOVIES AND SHOWS" | caption band | 369 px · 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 259 px |
| BLANK (6000–8000 ms) | caption band | no ink (scheduled blank) | — | — |
| L3 line 1 "HOWEVER, THE CURRENT CAPTIONING" | caption band | 521 px · 24 px (13.50 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 107 px |
| L3 line 2 "SYSTEM HAS SEVERAL SHORTCOMINGS" | caption band | 520 px · 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 108 px |
| L4 line 1 "THAT CAN MAKE THE VIEWING" | caption band | 421 px · 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 207 px |
| L4 line 2 "EXPERIENCE FRUSTRATING" | caption band | 368 px · 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 260 px |
| L5 "FOR DEAF AUDIENCES" (1 line) | caption band | 299 px · 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 329 px |
| swap L3 line 1 (71-char case, fitted fontPx 27.4) | caption band | 625 px · 24 px (13.50 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 3 px |
| swap L3 line 2 (fitted fontPx 27.4) | caption band | 525 px · 20 px (11.25 @360) | 628 px · band 64 px | 103 px |

Legibility floor (~11 px at 360 px stage): every measured line's ink height at 360 px is 11.25–13.50 px — PASS (floor met, thin margin +0.25 px on caps-only lines; the readability lens prices legibility in motion, which this leg does not own).
Two-line stack: 2 × 28 × 1.1 (CONFIG line-height factor) = 61.6 px ≤ 64 px band — fits with 2.4 px margin.
Hierarchy: single caption slot, one size per caption (fit-shrink varies it by ≤0.6 px across captions) — no hierarchy claimed, none to measure.

Icon geometry (renderer-matching projected bounds, HOLD cure 2 — `boundsFor` projects the map corners through CONFIG perspective + rotateY exactly as the renderer transforms them): at the camera scale peak (9500 ms) top −48.3 px (intentional top-edge crop, census f010) · bottom 264.3 px vs band limit 296 px. Whole-timeline sweep on a 100 ms grid (139 samples): max bottom 279.8 px, 0 band violations; min top −63.8 px (turn excursions only).

